"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-22T06:57:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-22T06:57:08Z","body":"> How do you ensure that **Preview** in the editor renders the materials / shaders?\n\nin my setup (linked MRP) i have the shader in front of the camera as a plane. like you would do post effects the \"old\" way:\n<img width=\"1202\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/009685bf-e266-4ebe-b68e-78ff7375e874\" />\nthis setup with MetalFX enabled and scale set to 0.5 already makes the shader purple in the viewport on my machine.\nthis is why it appears when the camera is selected and \"preview\" enabled.\n\ni assume it is getting wrong uv coordinates from the SCREEN_UV parameter, causing it to read outside of the available texture.\nbut only when DOF is enabled at the same time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2900127828/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2900133441","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106665#issuecomment-2900133441","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106665","id":2900133441,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6s3IZB","user":{"login":"thmasn","id":20150151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTUwMTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20150151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url"