thubusercontent.com/u/20150151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn","html_url":"https://github.com/thmasn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-22T07:11:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-22T07:23:32Z","body":"- as far as i can tell, the screenreading shader runs before the DOF.\n- as in the editor screenshot above, the issue only happens inside the plane using the shader.\n\n<img width=\"1202\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/009685bf-e266-4ebe-b68e-78ff7375e874\" />\n\n- this makes me assume that the pink is introduced by the screenreading shader.\n- but the built-in SCREEN_UV seems to provide correct uv coordinates, as i just tried out (uvs are over 0.5 halfway of the screen):\n\n<img width=\"472\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/740c173e-46b8-42b8-a016-abe3a390352f\" />\n\n- also, the texture is not pink yet inside the screen texture read (because this would trigger the r>.9 condition):\n\n<img width=\"592\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a6fbdf1-2148-4f1a-a42c-32d0281c9c9a\" />\n\n- but it is pink when it is beeing blended with the opaque objects? since tranparency lets opaque objects be visible in all of the screen:\n\n<img width=\"941\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85186ff1-c2fa-4050-b658-17674bb80141\" />\n\n- my best guess is that the issue appears somewhere in the auto-generated shader code, or maybe in a step that combines opaque + transparent obejcts","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2900159094/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2900186692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106665#issuecomment-2900186692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106665","id":2900186692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6s3VZE","user":{"login":"thmasn","id":20150151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTUwMTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20150151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn","html_url":"https://github.com/thmasn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thmasn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-22T07:24:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-22T07:24:48Z","body":"just noticed that it is also only on mobile renderer, forward+ works","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2900186692/react